description:
**Crédit Agricole Corporate and Investment Banking (Crédit Agricole** CIB) is the corporate and investment banking arm of Crédit Agricole Group, world’s 10th largest bank by total assets.


Our Singapore center **(“ISAP” or “Information Systems Asia Pacific”)** is the**2nd largest IT setup (after Paris Head Office) for Crédit Agricole CIB's worldwide** business. We work daily with international branches located in 30 markets by:


* Envisioning and preparing the Bank’s futures information systems


* Partnering and supporting core banking flagships and transverse areas in their large scale development projects


* Providing premium In\-house Banking applications


This unique positioning empowers us to bring our core banking business a sustainable competitive advantage on the market.


**Position**

**Vulnerability Management Expert**


**Data Security Services** team in Singapore is responsible for day\-to\-day operational services on the infrastructure of Europe (mainly France and UK) and Asia remotely from Singapore. France infrastructure represents approximately 80% of the worldwide production activities of CA\-CIB in Singapore.


Team works in **Asia and** **Europe time zones** and this role will be aligned primarily to **France, UK and SGP working hours** . Flexible rotations are allowed based on the nature of duties.


The **operational support of the team** covers the following technical scope:


* Vulnerability Management Service


* Endpoint Security technologies – Anti\-virus management, Host Intrusion Prevention System etc.


* Data Leak Prevention systems, Encryption Solutions: Disk Encryption, File and Folder encryption, Database Audit Monitoring solutions


* Phishing Prevention solutions.


**Main responsibilities for this Role**

* **Vulnerability Management Expert** is an individual role within the Data Security Services team and will be responsible for owning the Vulnerability Management. The individual is supported by platform teams for remediation actions.


* The position is pivotal for driving the process with various cross\-functional (transverse) IT teams.


* Person will be responsible for **following (but not limited to) responsibilities** in day\-to\-day work:


* **Focal point of contact for Vulnerability Management** and related topics\- a go\-to person for **consultation regarding the vulnerabilities** identified by the tool and guide \& assist Infrastructure and Application teams to remediate the vulnerabilities identified under their application/infrastructure scope.


* Person will be **responsible preparing the Vulnerability Management Plan** and the **executes plan** through all the phases of Vulnerability Management Lifecycle.


* Ensures that the **Vulnerability scans are scheduled, configured in tool and are executed** as per the schedule. Any failure of scans is to be investigated and schedule to re\-run;


* Conducts **periodical discovery of IT Assets** and ensures that identified assets are highlighted to CMDB owner for appropriate Asset tagging and also onboards the new asset in Vulnerability Management tool;


* Assess the identified vulnerabilities and **study \& understand the risk profile** , impact as per environmental context;


* **Lead the discussions with Infrastructure and Application teams** and advise them the relevance of vulnerability and help them understand the impact;


* Understand the **false positives reported and the technical limitations** of the environment and facilitate the process of Risk Acceptance.


* Person will be responsible to**liaise with various stakeholders** for proposing and maintaining the approvals for such cases;


* **Collaborate with Infrastructure teams** \- Windows, Unix, Networks etc. for the remediation of the identified vulnerabilities.


* Maintain the **Vulnerability Dashboard for the scope** and submits reports both of Technical teams and Management Reporting;


* Organize work in order to achieve compliance to **established KPIs for Vulnerability Management** and proactively work towards achieving the same. Maintain periodical reporting on the progress;


* **Escalate\- discuss and consult** \- as required to next levels and Management in timely manner;


* Provide **subject matter expertise** for the Vulnerability Management service;


* Lead the **Penetration testing remediation planning** with cross functional teams;


* Conduct new **threat exposure scanning** across the asset scope and advise the applicability and lead remediation exercises with cross functional teams;


* Participate in meetings with various stake holders as per the schedules;


* Liaise with different teams in different geographical zones;


* Propose, plan and execute Service improvements initiatives;


* Adhere to different policies set out by the organization;


* Prepare and provide different reports (weekly/monthly/ad\-hoc) to the Manager as necessary;


* Maintain appropriate knowledge required for successful and efficient delivery of the responsibilities;


* Keeping abreast of new threats and vulnerabilities and provide analysis as per applicability;


* Comply with all applicable legal, regulatory and internal Compliance requirements, including, but not limited to, the Singapore Compliance manual and Compliance policies and procedures as issued from time to time; Financial Security requirements, including, but not limited to, the prevention of Financial Crime and Fraud including reporting obligations to the Money Laundering Reporting Officer.


**Work Schedule**

Work schedule is mainly aligned to Asia and EMEA time zone. However, candidate may have to work outside of work\-hours for urgent or critical threat management topic as applicable and as required.


Flexible work schedule (based on roster) is followed:


* General hours: 10 AM – 7 PM or 11 AM – 8 PM SGT


* Afternoon hours: 12:00 Noon – 9 PM SGT (as per operations needs as required).


**Qualifications and Profile**

* **10 \-12 years of IT experience** with **6\-8 years of IT Security experience** and **5\+ years of experience in managing Vulnerability Management process** for an enterprise.


* Should be a **bachelors/masters/engineering graduate or equivalent technical degree** in Information Technology or Computer Science;


**Professional Certifications (highly preferred)**


* Certified Information Systems Security Professional **(CISSP)**
* GIAC Enterprise Vulnerability Assessor **(GEVA), or** any other Vulnerability Management Certification


* CREST certification


* Working \& **hands\-on experience** in managing Vulnerability Management process;


* Strong **technical understanding and experience** assessing vulnerabilities and identifying weaknesses in multiple operating system platforms, networks, database, and application servers.


* Ability to **assess vulnerabilities and prioritize remediation** planning;


* Experience in working **collaboratively with cross\-functional/transverse IT** teams in **Production setup** (Operations) mode;


* Ability to apply **Risk based approach** while working on assigned responsibilities;


* Must have working experience in **administrating and operating Tenable (Nessus) Security Center** vulnerability management tool for a Large enterprise level environment;


* Good understanding of **Reporting needs at various levels of organization** and ability to **design, create and present the same;**
* **Hands\-on experience of creating reports** using various tools such as Excel, PowerPoint, Word in graphical formats, trending;


* **Proficiency in Powershell or SQL query**
* Experience in **working with any BI tools** like Power BI etc. to prepare the dashboard;


* Knowledge of **different domains of Information Security** ;


* Working experience in **financial organization** is highly preferred;


* Excellent in **analytical, communication and documentation** skills;


* Ability to organize work and be **able to priories work** as per the Operation’s needs;


* Must have strong understanding of **ITIL processes** and comfortable working in process\-oriented environment;


* Ability to **work independently** and as well as a part of team and is able to work under **minimal supervision;**
* Should have **time management skills** and able to manage work in fast moving environment;


We seek innovative and agile people sharing our mindset to support ambitious and forthcoming technological challenges.


**Note \-**

* **This is a shift\-based role.**
* **This is 12 months contract role. Renewable subject to performance.**
We offer a competitive remuneration package, consistent with your qualifications and experience. For fair employment practices, we are keen on**Singaporeans/SPR ONLY.**


**Interested applicants, please click on "APPLY"**


Visit us on:


**http://www.ca\-cib.com/**

**Job Title**: Executive Assistant to General Manager  
**Reports to**: General Manager  
**Location**: Singapore  
**Industry**: Architectural Curtain Wall / Façade Engineering

**Position Overview**

We are representing a well\-established and competitive architectural curtain wall engineering company in search of a highly capable Executive Assistant to the General Manager. You will serve as a key strategic support to the GM, playing an important role in high\-level operational management, project coordination, and business advancement within the curtain wall industry.

**Key Responsibilities**

* Provide comprehensive executive support to the General Manager, including calendar management, meeting coordination, international travel arrangements, and priority management;
* Handle English and Chinese business correspondence, document drafting, report preparation, and follow\-up;
* Organize senior management meetings and project review sessions, prepare high\-quality minutes, and track action items;
* Coordinate communication with developers, main contractors, design institutes, material suppliers, and other external stakeholders;
* Support tender document preparation, contract review, technical documentation, and other project\-related administrative tasks in the curtain wall business;
* Assist with internal team management, cross\-departmental coordination, and project progress monitoring;
* Manage confidential documents and perform other ad\-hoc tasks as assigned by the General Manager.

**Requirements**

* Bachelor’s degree or above; major in Engineering Management, Business Administration, English, or related fields preferred;
* Minimum 5 years’ experience as Executive Assistant to GM or similar C\-level roles; experience in architectural curtain wall, façade, window \& door, steel structure, or construction industry is a strong advantage;
* Fluent in both spoken and written Chinese (Mandatory requirement – able to draft professional Chinese documents and meeting minutes);
* Good command of written and spoken English (able to handle bilingual business communication);
* Familiarity with curtain wall industry terminology and project workflow is highly preferred;
* Strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills with excellent attention to detail;
* Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint);
* High level of integrity, discretion, and professionalism.

**What We Offer**

* Competitive remuneration package (to be discussed during interview);
* Opportunity to work closely with senior leadership in the curtain wall industry;
* Stable career platform with good long\-term development prospects;
* Comprehensive benefits package.

Pay: $5,500\.00 \- $11,000\.00 per month

Benefits:

* Additional leave
* Employee assistance programme
* Health insurance
* Professional development
* Promotion to permanent employee
* Vision insurance

Work Location: In person

*Founded in 1913 in Italy, the Prada Group was built on a tradition of excellence and with a vision of innovation. The Group, a world leader in the luxury sector, operates in more than 45 countries with the PRADA, Miu Miu, Versace, Church’s, Car Shoe and Luna Rossa brands, and has employees of over 100 nationalities.* **JOB PURPOSE**

As Prada Client Advisor, You guarantee an extraordinary and memorable luxury customer experience, placing the Client above all, discovering their needs and expectations, fostering meaningful relationships, serving as a Brand Ambassador.  

You convey and promote the Brand philosophy and Values to the final Clients guiding them into the world of Prada Brands.  

You hold yourself accountable to achieve your individual and team sales target, acting as proactive player in ensuring the best service and responding to the customer needs for both in store and on ecommerce channel.  


**RESPONSIBILITIES**
* Place the Customer at the center, creating a welcoming environment and striving to meet their every need and request, providing them with an excellence service in accordance to the “client journey ceremony”;
* Be driven to exceed individual sales targets and maximize own sales performances contributing to the success of the entire store;
* Be driven to exceed KPI goals, ensuring the highest quality of sales and customer service;
* Demonstrate an excellence knowledge of the products as well as Prada history, culture and DNA;
* Capture Customer data into the Company CRM with the purpose of connecting to the client, maintaining and developing the relationships to offer a personalized approach and develop future opportunities;
* Embrace and promote the Omni Channel mindset;
* Build and maintain an ample knowledge of the world of luxury fashion by being constantly informed on fashion trends and competitors, with the purpose to be able to discuss them with the customers and to give advises;
* Take ownership of resolving Client complaints liaising with the line manager and Client Service team, when necessary;
* Operate with the highest level of care and respect for the Products;
* Utilize Company digital tools actively to offer a complete and integrated luxury experience;
* Host and conduct customer appointments either in presence or leveraging technology to do virtual meeting;
* Work in synergy with the Back of House, participating to the daily operations of the store and maintaining an organized stock room;
* Act in compliance to Company procedures on operational guidelines and stock procedures, as well as security, cash activity, inventory, logistics and all main reporting activities requested by head office, ensuring that Company policies and procedures are proactively executed;
* Work as a team player and partner with fellow colleagues, foster open and constructive communication, to ensure a consistent exceptional experience and contribute to a positive working environment, embracing Diversity and inclusion values.



**KNOWLEDGE AND SKILLS**
* Passion for human relations and sales
* Problem solving, curiosity and interest in luxury/fashion, art and design
* Experience of building a long\-lasting relationship with clients
* Being able to work in team as well as alone
* Excellent communication and interpersonal skills
* Passion and knowledge of the managed product category


\#LI\-AK1  


*Joining our Company means working in a creative and international environment, with teams of people motivated by curiosity and the quest for excellence. The engine of our success is the importance and value that we place on the talent and passion of our people leading to their own professional growth.*  

*Prada Group promotes an inclusive work environment, ensuring equal opportunities for all candidates, regardless of gender, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability, or other personal characteristics. We believe that diversity is a value and we are committed to build a fair and respectful workplace for all.*

**\[What the role is]**

As a Senior/ Assistant Director of General Investigations, you will be leading a team of investigation officers to undertake a range of challenging activities to safeguard public health.
**\[What you will be working on]**

General Investigations is responsible for the post\-marketing surveillance and enforcement activities of all health products (including but not limited to Therapeutic Products, Medical Devices, Chinese Proprietary Medicines, Traditional Medicines, Health Supplements and Cosmetics) in both the legal and illegal market to ensure that they meet the internationally benchmarked standards of safety and quality, so as to safeguard public health and safety. Additionally, General Investigations may also be tasked to undertake investigations into other health related matters as assigned by the management.


Reporting to the Deputy Director, General Investigations, the Senior/ Assistant Director is responsible in assisting to:


* Formulate, develop, implement and review enforcement policies and strategies to achieve effective enforcement outcomes;

* Ensure strategic manpower development, resources allocation and deployment programmes are effectively implemented in the Branch;

* Manage resources (including overseeing and managing a team of investigating officers) effectively and efficiently in order to maximise resources and productivity within budgets;

* Build rapport and foster good partnership through regular platforms with external stakeholders and law enforcement agencies;

* Coordinate and support ongoing networking across various forums regionally and internationally to strengthen anti\-counterfeiting and enforcement capabilities (WHO, ASEAN, etc)

* Consolidate and continually review SOPs internally

* Communicate \& effectively implement SOPs with external agencies, where applicable;

* Assist in developing and reviewing workflow and collaborations with other Groups, Departments, Divisons.

* Train officers on investigation activities;

* Lead, develop and provide operational directions to a team of Investigation Officers to:
* Assist departments to conduct investigations for possible contraventions under the various Acts and subsidiary legislation within the ambit of Health Sciences Authority (HSA)
* Liaise and collaborate with international police organisation (e.g. Interpol) and overseas counterparts in on investigation matters;
* Prepare investigation papers and put up the relevant submissions;
* Liaise with HSA’s prosecutorial team and/or Attorney General’s Chambers on investigation matters;
* Plan for inspections and enforcement checks, and participating in these enforcement operations;
* Arrest offenders and accused persons, if necessary;
* Execute warrant of arrest of offenders who fail to attend court;
* Assist in identifying areas where illegal activities can occur;
* Arrange meetings with external agencies to coordinate enforcement activities and provide situational updates;
* Assist in prosecution of cases in court when required

**\[What we are looking for]**

* Strong leadership and command ability to motivate the team;
* Adaptability and decisiveness in dynamic and uncertain situations;
* Able to withstand stress;
* Demonstrate commitment and passion to protect public health and safety
* Team player who is able to work independently;
* Physically fit and active;
* Good interpersonal, communication and investigative skills;
* Extensive enforcement background with experience in both investigations and operations in enforcement agencies.

**What you will be doing**

* Responsible for the Singapore local market retail coverage and channel construction and management, responsible for the corresponding sales assessment indicators and business indicators;
* Cooperate with the planning and execution of offline marketing activities and online digital marketing, cultivate the market, generate clues and drive sales in a targeted manner;
* Participate in the development of sales strategies for local consumer products, market segmentation and Omni\-channel management.
* Undertake regional sales tasks, be responsible for regional market development, channel planning and management, and tap market potential and sales growth points;
* Connected with agents and retailers in the region to ensure that the company's sales strategy and management strategy were implemented in the whole sales channel;
* Regularly analyzed and rearranged the regional business, optimized the channel structure, and improved the overall sales performance in the region;
* Maintain customer relationship and improve customer satisfaction;

Other daily work in the area.  

* 


**The successful candidate**

* Bachelor's degree or above, at least 15 years’ experience in channel management or sales management.
* Familiar with the business model and operation method of local channel;
* Strong communication skills, strong ability to resist pressure and self\-drive;
* Industry understanding, channel development and organizational capabilities.

**Responsibilities**

The Director / Managing Director is responsible for the overall strategy, operations, and financial performance of the LNG / LPG business. The role provides executive leadership across trading, terminal operations, safety, investment, and organizational management, ensuring sustainable growth, compliance, and value creation.


**Key Responsibilities**

* Define and execute medium\- and long\-term strategy and annual business plans;
* Take full P\&L accountability, including revenue, profit, cash flow, and returns;
* Adjust business strategy in response to market, price, and regulatory changes;
* Oversee procurement, sales, trading, and terminal operations;
* Develop upstream supply partnerships and downstream customer portfolios;
* Lead major commercial negotiations and long\-term contract decisions;
* Build and lead a high\-performing management team and talent pipeline;
* Report to the Board and shareholders; execute Board resolutions ;
* Manage relationships with regulators, government bodies, financial institutions, and strategic partners.

**Qualifications**

* Bachelor’s degree or above in Energy, Engineering, Economics, Management, or related fields.
* 10–15\+ years of experience in LNG / LPG, natural gas, or energy\-related industries.
* Proven senior leadership experience (GM, Deputy GM, BU Head, or equivalent).
* Strong understanding of LNG / LPG markets, pricing, and regulatory environment.
* Demonstrated strengths in strategy, execution, negotiation, and risk management.
* International exposure and English working proficiency preferred.


China Gas International Pte Ltd is the international trading center established by China Gas Holdings Limited in Singapore, in charge of the international trading of mainly LNG and LPG, with the potential to expand to other energy and chemical commodities.

**Excited to grow your career?**  



BBVA is a global company with more than 160 years of history that operates in more than 25 countries where we serve more than 80 million customers. We are more than 121,000 professionals working in multidisciplinary teams with profiles as diverse as financiers, legal experts, data scientists, developers, engineers and designers.


**About the job:**

Job Purpose \& Objectives


Work in the Operations Middle Office team in Singapore which handles predominantly Trade Finance, Guarantees, Loans and some Remittances;


Key Responsibilities


* To handle customer enquiries regarding mainly trade finance transactions; liaise with counterparties regarding documents’ discrepancies after checking by Hub/ back office.
* Remit Trade Finance documents and processing of loans (mainly trade\-related loans);
* Review of Midas system transactions and reconciliations after input by Hub;
* Prepare/check Guarantees Letters / fees invoices etc
* Funding for loan drawdown and rollover;
* Prepare instructions for Loans/Guarantees/Trade Finance for input by Hub;
* Setup/ create customer record in Midas and input all authorized signatories/ directors/ beneficiary owners;
* Download SWIFT AMH messages;
* Perform market price checks and enquiry in Trade Finance Registry;
* Check account opening forms and documents;
* Handle remittances \& provide month\-end bank statements to customers;
* Follow up un\-reconciled Nostro items with counterparties;
* Prepare reports required for regulatory or internal purpose;
* Handle audit confirmation requests from customers;
* Assist on World\-check and FIRCO checks as and when required;
* Assist on other duties/ reports or back\-up functions as assigned by the Head of Production Management.

Qualification \& Experience


* At least 6 \- 8 years hands\-on experience in Trade Finance;
* Experience in Loan administration;
* Bachelor Degree or Diploma in Banking / International Trade / Business Administration / Finance or similar.

Knowledge \& Skills


* UCP600 \& ISBP knowledge required.
* Able to handle full set of Import/ Export documents including LC and all related document checking, financing, discounting, advising, collection, SBLC etc.
* Good knowledge and familiarity with Singapore banking regulations/ practices and regulatory reporting requirements.
* PC skills – words, excel etc.
* Experience with transition to new system or project handling will be advantageous.



Language


Fluent in written and spoken English. Ability to converse in Mandarin is preferred.


Other Skills (e.g. Interpersonal, Communication etc)


* Strong interpersonal and communication skills;
* Customer\-oriented;
* Well\-organized and meticulous/ keen eyes for details;
* Self\-motivated and ability to work in a multi\-cultural environment;
* Strong team player with ability to work independently;
* Ability to work under pressure.

**Skills:**

Interpersonal Communication
